/**
 * @page topic_webcam Webcam Capture
 * @ingroup module_abstractions
 * @brief Camera discovery and frame capture through the media input layer.
 *
 * Webcam capture is one possible media source, not a requirement of the client.
 * The media layer probes devices, opens the selected source, negotiates a usable
 * format, and presents owned frames to the common pipeline.
 *
 * @section webcam_platform Platforms
 *
 * Native builds use the platform/FFmpeg input path appropriate to the host.
 * Browser and iOS builds use their own capture bridges and capability rules.
 * Device names, pixel formats, frame rates, and permissions are platform data;
 * callers must use the probing result rather than assuming a camera exists.
 *
 * @section webcam_lifecycle Lifecycle
 *
 * Create and configure the input before starting capture. Stop acquisition before
 * releasing its frame buffers or device resources. Producers hand frames to the
 * encoder/render pipeline and must preserve the ownership contract when a frame
 * is queued or dropped.
 *
 * @section webcam_testing Testing
 *
 * Test-pattern and file inputs cover the client pipeline without hardware.
 * Hardware camera behavior still depends on OS permissions, device drivers, and
 * the selected format; an automated build cannot prove every camera model.
 *
 * @see topic_client_capture
 * @see topic_video_frame
 */
